            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@ContextConfiguration"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " supports boolean "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "inheritLocations"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "inheritInitializers"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " attributes that denote whether resource locations or component classes and context initializers declared by superclasses should be inherited. The default value for both flags is "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "true"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". This means that a test class inherits the resource locations or component classes as well as the context initializers declared by any superclasses. Specifically, the resource locations or component classes for a test class are appended to the list of resource locations or annotated classes declared by superclasses. Similarly, the initializers for a given test class are added to the set of initializers defined by test superclasses. Thus, subclasses have the option of extending the resource locations, component classes, or context initializers."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "If the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "inheritLocations"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " or "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "inheritInitializers"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " attribute in "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@ContextConfiguration"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " is set to "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "false"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", the resource locations or component classes and the context initializers, respectively, for the test class shadow and effectively replace the configuration defined by superclasses."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "admonition",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Test configuration may also be inherited from enclosing classes. See "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@Nested"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " test class configuration"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "xref",
            "target": "testing/testcontext-framework/support-classes.html#testcontext-junit-jupiter-nested-test-configuration"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " for details."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null,
        "type": "note"
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "In the next example, which uses XML resource locations, the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ApplicationContext"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " for "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ExtendedTest"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " is loaded from "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "base-config.xml"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "extended-config.xml"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", in that order. Beans defined in "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "extended-config.xml"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " can, therefore, override (that is, replace) those defined in "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "base-config.xml"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". The following example shows how one class can extend another and use both its own configuration file and the superclass’s configuration file:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
